From f12a93058f0f800c87301b347d7c390d9cd206cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lotus Developer <dev@lotus.org>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: apply validation, hashing, and mempool hotpath
 micro-optimizations

Port non-consensus hot-path micro-optimizations from Lotus V2:
- Hardware carry-less multiplication (ARM64 PMULL vmull_p64 / x86_64 PCLMULQDQ) in GF(2^64) set reconciliation (set_reconciliation.cpp and v2_protocol_handler.cpp)
- Stack-allocated BLAKE3 TaggedHash single-shot update (<= 960B) and stack-allocated (< 253B) Merklix leaf hashing with static cached EmptyTxRoot/EmptyUtxoRoot
- Lower multi-threaded Schnorr batch verification threshold (>= 32 signatures, up to 16 threads) in BatchSigCollector::VerifyAll
- Lazy TxOverlayArena branch hashing + 16-shard parallel EnsureDigest, pre-reserved coin/outpoint vectors, and FreezeEpochBatch SubtreeA pre-warming
- Deferred CTxMemPool overlay removals (m_pending_overlay_removes) under ScopedSnapshotDefer with O(1) full-mempool clear
- Flat power-of-2 open-addressed hash tables (txid_table and inputs_seen) in MemPoolAccept::AcceptRawTxBatch
- Coalesced ValidationSignals::TransactionsAddedToMempoolBatch, PeerManager::RelayTransactionBatch, and PeerManager::MarkPeerKnownTxBatch
- Skip redundant CCoinsViewCache::AccessCoin height lookup in Chainstate::ConnectBlock when SEQUENCE_LOCKTIME_DISABLE_FLAG is set
- Fix offline branch height in validation_block_tests MinerTestingSetup::Block for from-genesis BIP34 enforcement
